<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donnubán mac Cathail</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 980</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donnubán mac Cathail was king of the Uí Fidgenti, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-limerick">County Limerick</a>, in the later 10th century. Allied with Ivar, the Norse king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>, he took part in the capture of Mathgamain, king of Munster, who was handed over to his enemies and killed in 976. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> avenged his brother, and Donnubán's descendants, the O'Donovans, took their surname from him.</p></div>
